HST Office: no OpenCL self-test when the office starts.

Upstream Desktop::Main calls CheckOpenCLCompute() after OnStartApp, on the main thread, before the
Start Center answers. With UseOpenCL on and no stored test result (every new profile), it runs
opencltest.exe (up to 10 s) and then loads share/opencl/cl-test.ods hidden and computes it with
OpenCL kernels. A fault in the driver during that test reaches vcl's signal handler inside
OpenCLInitialZone: on Windows it turns OpenCL off and calls TerminateProcess with the restart code,
so soffice.exe starts the office again at once. No dialog, no Windows event, no recovery data; the
session marker of the first start stays, and the next start only knows that the previous session
"was not closed".

Measured on Windows 11 25H2 (HST 1.0.1, NVIDIA OpenCL): the first start of a fresh profile loads
OpenCL.dll and the vendor driver, runs opencltest.exe and writes SelectedOpenCLDeviceIdentifier;
the Start Center shows "Not responding" while the test runs. An access violation injected into the
main thread during the test gave exit code 0x51, an immediate restart, no events, and a log of
"start", "previous session ended: not closed", "start": the record of error reports HSTO-000010
and HSTO-000011 (first start of a new profile, 31 s and 41 s before the restart).

HST Sheets never computes formulas with OpenCL (hst-sheets-error-parity.patch), and UseOpenCL is
off by default (StartupDefaults.xcu), but Expert Configuration or an administrator's configuration
can still turn UseOpenCL on, which would bring the test back at the next start. The test has no
purpose any more, so it is not called.

